---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { ONPREM } from "../lib/edition";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy notice for openrepairrecord.com: no account, no cookies, cookie-less visit counting; the builder runs in your browser." noindex>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    {ONPREM ? (
    <div class="prose" data-edition="onprem">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>This is a self-hosted copy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Your organisation runs this copy of Open Repair Record on its own server, and is responsible for it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The pages make <strong>no requests outside your network</strong>: no analytics, no fonts, no scripts or images from anywhere else.</li>
        <li>What you type into the builder is processed in your browser only. Your draft is kept in your browser's local storage, on your device; it is not stored on the server and not shared with colleagues.</li>
        <li>Files you open or download (JSON, PDF) are read and written on your device.</li>
        <li>Like any web server, the server may keep its own access logs. Ask your IT team how they are handled.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted">The authors of Open Repair Record receive nothing from this copy.</p>
    </div>
    ) : (
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lead">The short version: no account, no cookies, page views counted without tracking you, and the builder never sends what you type anywhere.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Dmytro Rybka, Im Hoffeld 31/1, 74427 Fichtenberg, Germany. E-mail:
        <a href="mailto:support@pmfriend.com">support@pmfriend.com</a>. See also the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens in your browser</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything you type into the builder is processed in your browser only. It is not sent to us or to anyone else.</li>
        <li>Your draft is kept in your browser's local storage, on your device, so it is still there when you come back. You can delete it at any time with "New blank record" or by clearing this site's data in your browser.</li>
        <li>Files you open or download (JSON, PDF) are read and written on your device.</li>
        <li>"Open in WhatsApp" opens WhatsApp with the message text, only when you click it. What happens next is between you and WhatsApp.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This site is static and is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., USA. When you open a page, your
        browser connects to GitHub's servers, which receive technical data such as your IP address, the page requested
        and your browser type. According to GitHub's privacy statement, GitHub may keep logs of visitor IP addresses for
        security and to comply with legal obligations. We do not receive these logs. The legal basis is our legitimate
        interest in delivering the site securely (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). For transfers to the USA, GitHub relies on the
        transfer mechanisms described in its
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Counting visits</h2>
      <p>
        To see which pages are read and where visitors come from, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics, a service of
        Cloudflare, Inc., USA. A small script reports each page view: the page, the referring site, and the browser,
        device type and country derived from the request. It sets no cookies, does not use local storage, does not
        follow you across sites and does not build a profile; we see only totals. The builder's content is never part
        of it. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). See
        Cloudflare's <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies, no cross-site tracking, no advertising.</li>
        <li>No fonts or images loaded from other services; the only outside script is the visit counter above.</li>
        <li>No newsletter and no forms that send data to us. If you e-mail us, we use your message only to reply.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data
        portability and objection. Write to the address above. You can also complain to a data protection supervisory
        authority, for example the one for Baden-Württemberg (Landesbeauftragter für den Datenschutz und die
        Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg).
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated: 18 October 2026 (visit counting added).</p>
    </div>
    )}
  </div>
</Base>
